● Here's the current state of the project:

  pdanet-client — Android VPN client that transparently routes traffic through PdaNet+'s WiFi Direct hotspot.

  Architecture:
  App traffic → TUN (VpnService) → tun2proxy (Rust) → HTTP proxy 192.168.49.1:8000 → PdaNet phone → Internet

  Current status per CLAUDE.md: FULLY WORKING (as of 2026-02-19 Session 2)

  Key files:
  - app/src/main/kotlin/tun/proxy/service/Tun2HttpVpnService.kt — Core VPN service, PdaNet detection, routing
  - app/src/main/kotlin/com/github/shadowsocks/bg/Tun2proxy.kt — JNI wrapper for libtun2proxy.so
  - app/src/main/kotlin/com/pdanetclient/ — MainActivity, BootReceiver, VpnPermissionActivity
  - app/src/main/jniLibs/*/libtun2proxy.so — Pre-built Rust native libs (arm64, armv7, x86, x86_64)

  How it works:
  1. Monitors WiFi for gateway 192.168.49.1 (PdaNet indicator)
  2. Auto-starts VpnService — TUN interface intercepts all traffic
  3. Routes exclude 192.168.0.0/16 to prevent routing loop (proxy connection goes via wlan0 directly)
  4. Virtual DNS (Fake-IP) maps domains to 198.18.0.0/15 for HTTP proxy compatibility
  5. Starts at boot, no ADB required after APK install

